          "C": "Research ARM64 four-core acceleration of dense DP without violating its left/up dependencies. Investigate tiled wavefront execution: tiles on the same tile anti-diagonal are independent once their top and left boundaries are available, while each tile performs an efficient sequential local recurrence. Keep boundary storage compact rather than requiring a full integer grid. Explore tile sizes, scheduling overhead, and a serial threshold under the existing compilation environment. An alternative is a row-wise segmented prefix scan with blocked cells resetting the sum; account for synchronization and extra passes before pursuing it. Benchmark end-to-end against optimized serial DP, not just the original.",
