    "synthesis": {
      "model_calls": 1,
      "phase": "synthesis",
      "plan": {
        "A": "Research obstacle storage and preprocessing for Problem D. Starting from d45f1ccb3f5a44cc, compare CSR sorted/deduplicated obstacle spans against packed masks, emphasizing compatibility with tiled traversal and avoiding quadratic obstacle allocation. Supply tile-clipped unobstructed spans without repeated full-row searches; preserve duplicate-coordinate semantics. Measure preprocessing plus computation, not just the inner loop.",
        "B": "Develop a reusable ARM64 NEON span kernel from 85e46eb73a754e3f for C's tile boundaries. Compare four-lane and 16-cell scans with scalar handling of short spans and tails. Preserve incoming left carry, return the final carry, and reset at every obstacle. Reduce every modular addition before subsequent scan stages; do not vectorize the original dependent recurrence naively. Measure standalone and tiled performance.",
        "C": "Refine e13961b2098a46bc as the leading parallel design. Explore tile dimensions and serial crossover for four cores, balancing available anti-diagonal concurrency, locality, and barrier costs. Preserve disjoint boundary ownership and barriers between diagonals. Retain 5a92fa3ecd804d20 as a competing pipeline rather than assuming it is inferior: its mean is only about 1.3% higher. Account for actual OpenMP team size and retain a correct non-OpenMP path.",
        "G": "Use e13961b2098a46bc as the incumbent. Integrate incrementally: buffered input, A's obstacle representation, then B's span kernel inside C's schedule. Measure each combination under the unchanged harness and retain the fastest validated complete program; also compare the pipeline alternative. Do not mechanically merge overlapping solution.cpp replacements or assume gains multiply. Check n=1, blocked endpoints, duplicate obstacles, first-row/column barriers, partial tiles, SIMD tails, modular wraparound, and thread-boundary dependencies. Change only permitted program source, never tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions.",
        "analysis": "The supplied source solves Problem D, not the other contest problems. Its quadratic DP has a horizontal dependency, per-cell obstacle checks and remainder operations, plus row copying. On this ARM64 four-core run, tiled C leads at 13.843 ms versus the 81.483 ms baseline, approximately 5.89x faster; pipeline C follows at 14.023 ms. Unrolled NEON B takes 20.643 ms, while A's packed-row and span variants take 22.767 and 23.466 ms. These measurements favor parallel scheduling as the integration foundation, with sparse obstacle handling and SIMD as independently measured additions. Candidate timing variability and combination performance are unknown. Correctness requires exact modular path counting on every valid input; reduced residues make a two-term sum safe in signed 32-bit arithmetic, but longer unreduced scans do not."
      },
